    <bpmn:process id="W_W1816" name="W1816. Emergency Capex Request Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Urgent capital need (equipment failure, safety issue, storm damage, regulatory order)
Frequency: ~5–10 emergency requests/year
Volume: Low volume but time-critical
Owner: Department Head
Participants: Department Head, CEO, CFO
Source: workflow W1816 — Emergency Capex Request Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1816_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1816_Lane1" name="Department Head">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1816_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1816_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1816_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1816_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1816_Lane2" name="CEO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1816_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1816_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1816_Start4" name="Urgent capital need (equipment failure, safety issue, storm damage, regulatory order)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1816_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1816_Task5" name="Emergency triggers: (a) store HVAC failure in summer (cannot operate without…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Emergency triggers: (a) store HVAC failure in summer (cannot operate without cooling in Philippine heat), (b) typhoon damage to store structure, (c) forklift failure at DC (halts operations), (d) BIR order to upgrade POS system (compliance deadline), (e) fire damage to store or DC
Responsible (R): Department Head
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Immediate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1816_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1816_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1816_Task6" name="Department Head contacts CEO/CFO directly (phone/email): (a) describes…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Department Head contacts CEO/CFO directly (phone/email): (a) describes emergency, (b) estimated cost, (c) business impact of delay, (d) proposed solution and timeline
Responsible (R): Department Head
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1816_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1816_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1816_Task7" name="CEO provides verbal approval; CFO authorizes emergency procurement: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: CEO provides verbal approval; CFO authorizes emergency procurement: (a) procurement can proceed without full financial evaluation (W1812 bypassed), (b) PO issued with emergency flag, (c) retroactive documentation completed within 5 business days (full capex request, financial evaluation, formal approval)
Responsible (R): CEO / CFO
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Same day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1816_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1816_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1816_Task8" name="Retroactive formal approval completed; project entered in system with…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Retroactive formal approval completed; project entered in system with &quot;Emergency&quot; designation; Board informed at next meeting if amount &gt; PHP 10M
Responsible (R): Department Head / FP&amp;A
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Within 5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1816_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1816_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1816_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1816_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1816_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-361 (ensure controlled execution — Capital Expenditure Request &amp; Approval (PA-40.1).) | - operational: Department Head review and approval gate
Owner: Department Head</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
